+# Feature: Threshold Support for frai eval ✓ COMPLETE
+
+## Summary
+Successfully implemented threshold support for `frai eval` command, allowing CI/CD pipelines to gate on evaluation metrics. The feature is production-ready and fully tested.
+
+## Requirements Met
+
+### ✓ CLI Option
+- `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option implemented
+- Can be specified multiple times (e.g., `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.8`)
+- Documented in help text: "Can be specified multiple times"
+
+### ✓ Threshold Validation
+- Format validation: `metric=number` format required
+- Range validation: minimum value must be 0-1
+- Metric validation: metric ID must exist in evaluations
+- Error handling: Clear error messages listing valid metric IDs
+
+### ✓ Exit Codes
+- **Exit 0**: All thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified)
+- **Exit 1**: Any threshold fails (metric score < minimum)
+- **Exit 2**: Usage error (malformed format, invalid range, unknown metric)
+
+### ✓ Null Score Handling
+- Metrics with null/undefined scores fail their thresholds
+- Prevents false positives when metrics can't be computed
+- Example: exact_match with no references returns null score → fails threshold
+
+### ✓ Report Formats
+
+#### JSON Reports
+```json
+{
+  "passed": true|false,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": 1,
+      "passed": true
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+#### Markdown Reports
